      "answer_text": "**Interval:** 120,000 ms (120 s). It's `HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS = 120_000` at `.opencode/plugins/context-engineering.ts:138`.\n\n**What it does:** the `setInterval` at `context-engineering.ts:185-187` sends `{ type: \"heartbeat\", session_id: id }` to the bridge for every session the plugin has seen. The timer is `unref()`'d at line 188, so it doesn't keep the process alive.\n\n**Why it's needed:**\n- Each session has a memory-only retention lease in the Python bridge. Every normal request renews it.\n- Without any sign of life, the lease lapses after 300 s. The stored reference then expires after another 300 s (`README.md:107-109`).\n- A user can go quiet for a long time between turns, and a stored reference may be read back many turns later. The heartbeat keeps the lease alive during that silence.\n- 120 s is well inside the 300 s window, so one or two missed beats don't lose the lease. A test asserts this (`context-engineering.test.ts:281-283`)."
    },
